# Sanctioned mess — never committed
scratch/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Contact details live here, never in git. resume.json holds achievements only.
src/contact.json
!src/contact.example.json

# board-health.tsv is NOT ignored. A CI runner is thrown away after every job, so
# ignoring it would mean the scheduled scans record nothing, and it is append-only
# observation that cannot be reconstructed later. jobs.tsv is not here either — it
# is the application record and the only copy.

# Dependencies / build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Rendered resumes carry contact details, and they are reproducible: a tracked
# selection.json plus resume.json and contact.json regenerate any of them
# exactly. So the selections are kept and the renders are not.
#
# Deliberately near the end: git takes the last matching rule, and a broad `out/`
# rule would untrack every selection.json — the one artifact here worth keeping.
out/**/*.pdf
out/**/*.html

# src/postings/ is tracked (decision 020). The store is primary, perishable data:
# the text of a delisted posting cannot be re-fetched, and a stored posting never
# changes, so each appears in exactly one diff.

# The duty bank is derived, not observed. It is regenerated from src/postings/ with
# `node src/mine-duties.mjs`, and tracking it would put a large, rewritten-daily
# file into permanent git history.
src/duty-bank.json

# The shortlist is derived and regenerated whole every run (spec 006 R12).
# Committing it would rewrite every line daily.
out/shortlist/

# The backfill writes this beside jobs.tsv as belt-and-braces for the moment of
# the rewrite. Git already holds the pre-change ledger, so tracking it would mean
# a second, immediately-stale copy of the application record.
src/jobs.tsv.bak
